### **Do's:**
✅ Use environment-specific `.env` files (`.env.development`, `.env.production`)  
✅ Validate all required secrets at application startup  
✅ Use a secrets manager in production  
✅ Rotate secrets regularly  
✅ Never log or expose secrets in error messages  
✅ Encrypt secrets at rest and in transit  
✅ Use least-privilege IAM roles for secret access  
✅ Implement secret versioning  
✅ Monitor for secret access and unauthorized usage  

### **Don'ts:**
❌ Commit `.env` files to version control  
❌ Hardcode secrets in source code  
❌ Store secrets in comments or documentation  
❌ Use the same secrets across environments  
❌ Share secrets via email or chat  
❌ Embed secrets in client-side code  
❌ Use weak or predictable secrets  

