## 📋 **Secret Management Security Checklist**

| Practice | Status | Why It Matters |
|----------|--------|----------------|
| Never commit `.env` files to version control | ❌ Critical | Prevents secrets from being exposed in Git history |
| Use secrets manager (Vault, AWS SM, Azure Key Vault) | ❌ Missing | Centralized audit, rotation, access control |
| Rotate secrets regularly | ❌ Not implemented | Limits impact if secrets are compromised |
| Use different secrets per environment | ❌ Not applicable | Prevents cross-environment exposure |
| Encrypt secrets at rest | ❌ Not applicable | Protection if storage is breached |
| Implement secret access logging | ❌ Not applicable | Audit trail for compliance |
| Use short-lived credentials where possible | ❌ Not implemented | Reduces attack window |

